# Task 4 report — rich causal diagnostics

## Outcome

Implemented the optimizer V5 causal diagnostics/report adapter in the three authorized source
files. No test file was created or modified, and `evaluator.py` did not require a scope expansion:
its existing injected `EvaluationReportBuilderV5` accepts `summarize_panel_result` directly.

## Engine evidence

- Added frozen, slotted `PositionEpisode` evidence only to `SimulationResultV5`. Each episode binds
  a stable local episode ID, entry/exit symbol and session, actual execution prices, causal maximum
  and minimum completed-bar marks, fill-cash realized return, immutable quantity-change path,
  add-on count, holding sessions, and terminal exit reason.
- Completed-bar extrema are updated only in the V5 after-close phase. Opening-gap and next-open
  exits therefore cannot consume incomplete current-bar highs/lows. Terminal last-close positions
  include the completed terminal bar before liquidation.
- Every V5 close path funnels through episode finalization. Terminal liquidation now fails closed
  if any position or episode state remains because its final price evidence was unavailable.
- Identity transitions remap the open episode state together with the trade while preserving the
  entry identity. Fill rows bind to a stable `EpisodeId`, allowing exact per-position cash-flow and
  quantity reconciliation without ticker guessing.
- V5 fill rows now carry stop-reference kind and stop price. Gap shortfall is therefore measured
  from the actual causal gap-open reference rather than reconstructed from later data.
- Added frozen daily `PortfolioObservationV5` rows containing session cash, close-marked gross
  long notional, total equity, and O'Neil regime. The engine verifies cash plus gross notional equals
  the daily equity mark and rewrites the terminal observation after last-close liquidation.
- Added V5-only policy-intent outcome counts for queued, next-open executed, missing-open delay
  sessions, stop-preempted, and terminally unexecuted intents. Conservation is checked in the report.
- Episode state, completed episodes, daily observations, and policy-intent counts round-trip through
  the schema-V5 checkpoint/state journal. Legacy schema 4 and `SimulationResult` remain untouched.

The current engine has no add-on/pyramiding carrier. Episodes therefore record `add_on_count=0`
today, while the evidence schema and BUY-fill reconciliation require one initial BUY plus exactly
the declared number of future add-ons. No synthetic add-on evidence was fabricated.

## Report builder and reconciliation

`core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py` provides the exact Task 3 adapter signature:

```python
summarize_panel_result(*, panel, scenario, result) -> EvaluationReportV5
```

It populates every `EvaluationReportV5` field:

- net portfolio total/CAGR, cost-restated gross diagnostic CAGR, benchmark total/CAGR, max
  drawdown, daily Sharpe, closed trades, average exposure/cash, and fill turnover;
- total friction and exact gross-minus-net return drag;
- win rate, average win/loss, payoff, expectancy, and median completed holding sessions;
- exposure-normalized invested-sleeve CAGR estimate and the corresponding idle-cash drag;
- stop-gap dollar shortfall, transfer count, scale-out opportunity cost, and MFE/MAE quartiles;
- stage/outcome/regime/episode/source-universe entry funnel counts, exit attribution, and policy
  intent outcomes;
- chained regime slices, the panel episode slice, calendar-year slices, and monthly endpoint
  rolling 12/24/36-month returns whenever sufficient history exists.

All report numerics cross into immutable contracts as finite `Decimal` values. Money is reconciled
at cents and reported at cents; other report boundaries use deterministic six-decimal precision.
The net scenario remains the selection evidence. Gross is an explicit cost add-back diagnostic,
not an alternate selection objective.

The adapter rejects rather than defaults when any of the following evidence differs: authenticated
panel sessions versus portfolio/benchmark curves; observations versus daily equity; terminal cash
versus ending equity; scenario identity; fill schema or recomputed `apply_friction` values; fill-row
costs versus aggregate/config totals; episode IDs, dates, execution prices, quantities, realized
returns, or closed trades; initial cash plus fill cash versus terminal equity; entry outcomes versus
engine diagnostic counts; policy-intent conservation; and signal symbol/session versus the panel
and regime observations. Mathematically undefined trade metrics remain `None` only for genuine
zero-observation cases.

## Provider projection

Added frozen `RoleEvidenceItemV5` and `RoleEvidenceV5` contracts and
`to_role_evidence(report)`. The projection:

- contains aggregate scalar, distribution, attribution, slice, latest rolling, and funnel values;
- uses deterministic semantic evidence IDs and canonical JSON identity;
- is capped at 96 items and 16 KiB;
- contains no raw ticker rows, raw per-session rows, local paths, credentials, or provider payloads;
  rolling evidence is exposed by window rather than by raw end-session date; and
- truncates only after higher-priority scalar, excursion, exit/policy, slice, and rolling evidence,
  then bounded funnel evidence.

