### Direct deterministic engine episode smoke

Two real V5 simulator-internal lifecycles used `apply_friction`, completed-bar marking, and the
central close method. One closed at 110 after a 120/95 completed range and one at a 90 stop after a
105/80 range. Both finalized immutable zero-ending quantity paths and one completed holding session:

```text
[('position-00000001', 9.890054972513749, 1, 120, 95),
 ('position-00000002', -10.089955022488759, 1, 105, 80)]
```

### Deterministic winner/loser report smoke

An 800-session provider-free synthetic report used one winner, one loser, two regimes, four
calendar years, one authenticated ticker transfer, exact base-scenario fills, and explicit terminal
cash/exposure observations. It also substituted the digest of diagnostics bytes plus one extra byte
to prove evaluator source identity changes. Output:

```json
{"cash":"97.963447","drag":"0.001000","expectancy":"-0.099950","exposure":"2.036553","friction":"2.00","holding":"15.000000","mae_min":"-20.039980","mfe_max":"19.940030","mismatch_failed_closed":true,"role_bytes":11706,"role_items":96,"rolling_windows":[12,24,36],"slice_counts":[2,4],"source_sha256":"9f32254a0050d93f8f483dab3ef60b4333b4877470c2b863263c6488d77aba18","stable_role_sha256":"cda346cb87e204fb85af88bc4970f7a5af9ffa0320154a5d92a39a1b857bade1"}
```

Assertions covered exact expectancy, MFE/MAE, holding median, friction/drag, entry funnel,
exit attribution, policy outcomes, exposure plus cash equaling 100%, regime/calendar/episode slices,
12/24/36-month rolling output, stable role IDs/digest, item/byte limits, absence of ticker/session/path
leakage, source-map resolution and byte sensitivity, cost-mismatch fail closure, and absence of V5
episode attributes on legacy `SimulationResult`.

A separate no-activity smoke returned genuine `None` for trade/excursion/sleeve metrics, zero idle
cash drag, and otherwise complete zero-count evidence (`ZERO_ACTIVITY_REPORT_OK`).

