## Review fix — exact episode transition reconciliation

The review found that the initial report builder reconciled episode-level buy/sell totals and the
coarse quantity-path shape, but did not replay each immutable quantity transition against the fill
rows carrying the same `EpisodeId`. The focused fix remains confined to
`core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py`.

Before any report metrics are produced, diagnostics now preserves fill-log row order and replays
every episode from zero quantity. Each BUY must map to `entry` or `add_on`; each SELL must map to
`scale_out` or terminal `exit`; and each path item must agree with its fill's session, reason,
execution price, and cumulative post-fill quantity. The replay also requires causal panel-session
order, exact fill/path cardinality, unique fill transitions, a fully closed terminal quantity,
the declared add-on count, and entry/exit sessions, symbols, execution prices, and exit reason that
match the first and last fills. Missing, extra, duplicate, reordered, cross-episode, or numerically
inconsistent transition evidence therefore fails closed before report construction. Reference-price
integrity continues to be enforced by the preceding friction replay in `_validate_fills`.

Direct provider-free smoke evidence:

```text
QUANTITY_PATH_RECONCILIATION_OK valid=winner+loser rejected=action,session,price,signed_delta,cumulative,duplicate_fill,reordered_fill,exit_reason
```

